<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §2, Tier 4 — the deep live-pattern metal.
       ParentName="ResourceBase" carrying deepCommonality/deepCountPerPortion/
       deepLumpSizeRange, the exact vanilla shape confirmed on Steel itself
       (mcp__rimsage__get_def_details Steel: deepCommonality 4,
       deepCountPerPortion 45, deepLumpSizeRange 20~30) and on
       ThingDef.cs:1856-1862 (the engine enforces the pair being set
       together). Drilling it is what arms §5 (the deep-drill response
       event) — the incident worker itself lives in §5's own build, not
       here.

       "Cathedral map gen only" (kit spec): unlike Tiers 1-3, vanilla's deep
       resource pick has NO biome axis at all to restrict against —
       measured via rimsage source read of RimWorld/CompDeepScanner.cs:
       `ChooseLumpThingDef()` returns
       `DefDatabase<ThingDef>.AllDefs.RandomElementByWeight(d => d.deepCommonality)`,
       a flat GLOBAL weighted pool over every ThingDef with deepCommonality
       set, read fresh on every scan with no per-map or per-biome filter
       anywhere in the call chain (Verse/DeepResourceGrid.cs has no
       generation-time population step either — the grid is populated
       lazily, only by a scan or a drill, never by a GenStep at map
       creation). This repo's two existing biome-exclusive deep resources
       (Kyber, Pyrinth — LanternDeeps/Patches/RUT_LanternDeepGateKyber.xml,
       RUT_LanternDeepGatePyrinth.xml) solve the equivalent "universal
       leak" by zeroing the field and re-adding it only via a GenStepDef
       that is referenced solely from Lantern Deeps' own dedicated
       MapGeneratorDef — a trick that only works because pocket maps get
       their own generator. The Rust Cathedral is an ordinary overworld
       biome sharing the game's shared player map generator with every
       other biome, so that trick has no equivalent here.

       RESOLUTION: deepCommonality is left set (this def participates in
       the normal weighted pool like any deep resource), and
       Source/HarmonyPatch_GateLivePatternMetal.cs — a ~15-line postfix on
       CompDeepScanner.ChooseLumpThingDef — substitutes vanilla Steel
       whenever the result is this def and the scanning map's biome is not
       RUT_RustCathedral. This is the one place in this §2 slice that could
       not stay at the kit spec's own "zero new C#" hope; it is the same
       category of small, necessary, self-gated deviation the biome-gated
       GenStep subclasses below already needed for Tiers 1-3, just aimed at
       a different vanilla entry point because deep resources have no
       GenStepDef of their own to gate.

       INVENTED (kit spec): deepCountPerPortion 35. deepCommonality 4 and
       deepLumpSizeRange 10~20 are this build's own picks — no target given
       — set to feel notably rarer per lump than Steel's 20~30 while
       staying commonality-comparable so it is not vanishingly unlikely to
       actually appear once a Cathedral scan/drill occurs. -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_LivePatternMetal</defName>
    <label>live pattern metal</label>
    <description>Deep under the deck plate, past everything already dug, this metal is not dead. Nothing about the readout explains what it is doing, only that it is still doing it. Whoever pulls it out should be ready for what pulling it out means.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/Steel</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(196,168,74)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <deepCommonality>4</deepCommonality>
    <deepCountPerPortion>35</deepCountPerPortion>
    <deepLumpSizeRange>10~20</deepLumpSizeRange>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>14</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.5</Mass>
      <Beauty>-2</Beauty>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
